    "conclusion": "Corwin-Schultz FAILS the spec's own anchor by ~8x. The reason is identified, not guessed: 45-65% of its daily estimates are negative, so on these instruments it is pure noise floored at zero, and across tickers it correlates +0.95 with volatility but only +0.12 with log ADV -- it measures volatility, not liquidity. Abdi-Ranaldo (2017) and Roll (1984) fail identically. Daily-bar estimators were built for an era of 20-100 bps single-stock spreads; 1-3 bps ETF spreads are below their resolution.",
